{"title":"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Diagram\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/b/b6b5b6b078188523fb69a22aff2fbd2b3df42b14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB = 10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/c/15ce28968754a7ce34595935f04929c46f99d0e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"71\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/d/3/dd3b56dd066624723ac5dd1f64e2c45980c06984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be a point on segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" />. Let points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/f/e4f8fcfe896fcde9d2732076f4f3c3a94cf78f14.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/4/784f7f7f7228d0a77323715dca18f50aee49eb8c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I_C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> denote the incenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/a/a6adfd3ad27a2dddeb0af7131d73c33c86991e93.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/e/6ce2cd123db24a7b8373999aea7a98927e3b3c81.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ACD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"45\" height=\"14\" />, respectively. The circumcircles of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5ca7a11210ccab06db17e26d7bd7c54c14f58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI_BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9c63ddc0e6b1d95690854e44cd300530887011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI_CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" /> meet at distinct points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The maximum possible area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> can be expressed in the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/7/967433c8c2d5787f47a5609804fb21b06b22a8ec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a - b\\sqrt {c}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"63\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/d/2cdfeae33c1e09de6207d446beb72396c04be481.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a + b + c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"16\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram\">Diagram</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/a/6dace27445a7c58f5a24b097dff8d40104c5636e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] defaultpen(fontsize(11)+0.8); size(300); pair A,B,C,D,Ic,Ib,P;  A=MP(&quot;A&quot;,origin,down+left);  C=MP(&quot;C&quot;,8*right,down+right);  B=MP(&quot;B&quot;,IP(CR(A,5), CR(C,7)),2*up);   real t=0.505;  D=MP(&quot;&quot;,C+t*(B-C),SW);   draw(A--B--C--A--D);   path c1=incircle(A,D,C);  path c2=incircle(A,D,B);  draw(c1, gray+0.25);  draw(c2, gray+0.25);   Ic=MP(&quot;I_C&quot;,incenter(A,D,C),left);  Ib=MP(&quot;I_B&quot;,incenter(A,D,B),down+left);   path c3=circumcircle(Ic,D,C);  path c4=circumcircle(Ib,D,B);  draw(c3, fuchsia+0.2);  draw(c4, fuchsia+0.2);   P=MP(&quot;P&quot;,IP(c3,c4),up);   draw(arc(circumcenter(B,C,P),C,B), royalblue+0.5+dashed);  draw(C--Ic--D--P--C^^P--Ic, black+0.3);  draw(B--Ib--D--P--B^^P--Ib, black+0.3);   label(&quot;10&quot;,A--B,up+left);  label(&quot;16&quot;,A--C,down); [/asy]\" width=\"502\" height=\"332\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Law_of_Cosines\" title=\"Law of Cosines\">Law of Cosines</a>, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/0/c401dcde5f770cb7163e9688802e3532282003c6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos BAC = \\frac {16^2 + 10^2 - 14^2}{2\\cdot 10 \\cdot 16} = \\frac {256+100-196}{320} = \\frac {1}{2},\\]\" width=\"415\" height=\"39\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/7/757956f190570a9e1ac1665bff7eec4fa3d91759.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAC = 60^\\circ$\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/1/3216e8846eb44f1055c322fb5bd30169d5d62cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee48e5d3968014ef1e27c31e56d2f7ea5f8cb1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> be the circumcenters of triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/5/9f5ca7a11210ccab06db17e26d7bd7c54c14f58f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI_BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"49\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/9/5a9c63ddc0e6b1d95690854e44cd300530887011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI_CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"48\" height=\"15\" />, respectively.  The circles make us think of constant angles, so we first compute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/b/efb6647de5a652a58a342279b33aa757d1d783bd.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BO_1D = \\angle BO_1I_B + \\angle I_BO_1D = 2\\angle BDI_B + 2\\angle I_BBD.\\]\" width=\"441\" height=\"15\" /> Because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/e/f2efbe90a656cab4577e76f7540cc0581f309f9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDI_B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"61\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/1/361a71e7ee5c3b722b0f38cf037c6d10ffa0557c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle I_BBD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" /> are half of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/7/62778c987facd63dd959286c9d4ab82d6b641c25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BDA$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93e72b9d2c86f197276a931aba77c472d0511c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ABD$\" width=\"56\" height=\"13\" />, respectively, the above expression can be simplified to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/625c5213303bb4b295b1f35c093380014971ffe5.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle BO_1D = \\angle BO_1I_B + \\angle I_BO_1D = 2\\angle BDI_B + 2\\angle I_BBD = \\angle ABD + \\angle BDA.\\]\" width=\"576\" height=\"16\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/e/c9ecf25bb3c532e46c3dd104c196ece042ce7513.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CO_2D = \\angle ACD + \\angle CDA$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"223\" height=\"15\" />.  As a result\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/f/9df7d4d7e95e51f300e6867261f85ba931cadcbb.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*}\\angle CPB &amp;= \\angle CPD + \\angle BPD \\\\&amp;= \\frac {1}{2} \\cdot \\angle CO_2D + \\frac {1}{2} \\cdot \\angle BO_1D \\\\&amp;= \\frac {1}{2}(\\angle ABD + \\angle BDA + \\angle ACD + \\angle CDA) \\\\&amp;= \\frac {1}{2} (2 \\cdot 180^\\circ - \\angle BAC) \\\\&amp;= \\frac {1}{2} \\cdot 300^\\circ = 150^\\circ.\\end{align*}\" width=\"398\" height=\"191\" />\n</p><p>Therefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/f/01f0c60e1aa248980af3243a3bc4feaaf3de9cfc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPB$\" width=\"55\" height=\"12\" /> is constant (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/d/acd96fce8011b053b9d83a5b2d39ec3c756f0f66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$150^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"37\" height=\"15\" />). Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. Let point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> be on the same side of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c424736da27b2837f4a9b97c35b9b28af193fd33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LC = LB = BC = 14$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"173\" height=\"13\" />; <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on the circle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> as the center and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/7/d17cae39efb14f6f5c4ea1262bc5323746dd3dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{LC}$\" width=\"27\" height=\"15\" /> as the radius, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. The shortest (and only) distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/7/a0716a46782348fa29cc22d344f1b76a845f113a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"35\" height=\"21\" />.\n</p><p>When the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is the maximum, the distance from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> has to be the greatest. In this case, it's <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/c/95cf8a9a214d5087e0946d40c2d463fecbbfb0c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 - 7\\sqrt {3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. The maximum area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/2/822fa7991d01b3eeb4e7241a0f0573908adb97bf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac {1}{2} \\cdot 14 \\cdot (14 - 7\\sqrt {3}) = 98 - 49 \\sqrt {3}\\]\" width=\"251\" height=\"37\" />\nand the requested answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e3244ad074665a8690b7362ae5388d98e165f810.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98 + 49 + 3 = \\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/1/7f1814e815c82df409a161108a9ca17c22086605.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\cos{A}=\\frac{16^2+10^2-14^2}{2\\cdot 10\\cdot 16}=\\frac{1}{2}\\implies\\angle{A}=60^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"357\" height=\"39\" /> Setting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1ee7f0cbf77fb8c032159351b34750e3b613809c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{DAC}=\\theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" /> and doing some angle chasing, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/0/b40b5e4d0af184da414b1eaa899cd7bd6e2eb737.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{CI_CD}=\\frac{\\theta}{2}+90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"149\" height=\"39\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/3/7f38eeba72f4d1a4babbc95418052990201233e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{BI_BD}=\\frac{\\angle{A}-\\theta}{2}+90^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"203\" height=\"39\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/9/9a95030f53270af97b5657ab7739525848d4e1e9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle{CI_CD}+\\angle{BI_BD}=180^\\circ+\\frac{\\angle{A}}{2}=210^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"320\" height=\"37\" />Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/f/e1f7e985f73bcd65469b452cc75cde52e102e8f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CI_CDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/0/b8080f5fd78ec47c0c67dbd163b23bb1b3c5d9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI_BDP$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"63\" height=\"15\" /> are cyclic quadrilaterals, it follows that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/f/66fc969c50de09844786001ae95a4056aae6a08c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\angle{BPC}=\\angle{CPD}+\\angle{DPB}=(180^\\circ-\\angle{CI_CD})+(180^\\circ-\\angle{BI_BD})=360^\\circ-210^\\circ=150^\\circ.\\]\" width=\"668\" height=\"18\" />Next, applying Law of Cosines on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798f70b65f0016add81ae8fafe18f8fc5a3ff909.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{CPB}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" />,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/b/3eb1686770112f7e853c49e5bffa4d5fa1b30c95.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp; BC^2=14^2=PC^2+PB^2+2\\cdot PB\\cdot PC\\cdot\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ &amp; \\implies \\frac{PC^2+PB^2-196}{PC\\cdot PB}=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ &amp; \\implies \\frac{PC}{PB}+\\frac{PB}{PC}-\\frac{196}{PC\\cdot PB}=-\\sqrt{3} \\\\ &amp; \\implies PC\\cdot PB = 196\\left(\\frac{1}{\\frac{PC}{PB}+\\frac{PB}{PC}+\\sqrt{3}}\\right). \\end{align*}\" width=\"359\" height=\"190\" /> By AM-GM, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/0/36026487ad96ff7865356b80cb14eeaea2d7f22e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{PC}{PB}+\\frac{PB}{PC}\\geq{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"120\" height=\"37\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/e/d6e867f85191dfe46d50110fb1cbfb6f8ff0aa30.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[PB\\cdot PC\\leq 196\\left(\\frac{1}{2+\\sqrt{3}}\\right)=196(2-\\sqrt{3}).\\]\" width=\"335\" height=\"43\" />Finally, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/7/717bb862a397fa930b7ee1438db0381a22b6b298.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[\\triangle{BPC}]=\\frac12 \\cdot PB\\cdot PC\\cdot\\sin{150^\\circ}=\\frac14 \\cdot PB\\cdot PC,\\]\" width=\"386\" height=\"37\" />and the maximum area would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a05b7e33691fa5c25da9656fabf7247c494354c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$49(2-\\sqrt{3})=98-49\\sqrt{3},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"202\" height=\"24\" /> so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/4/4649b1f9c320291995474a6d45af1bf004dc433f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Proceed as in Solution 2 until you find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694edce082702c815ff46702afad805ecebea666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPB = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />. The locus of points <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> that give <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694edce082702c815ff46702afad805ecebea666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPB = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" /> is a fixed arc from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> will move along this arc as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> moves along <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />) and we want to maximise the area of [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />]. This means we want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to be farthest distance away from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> as possible, so we put <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in the middle of the arc (making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> isosceles). We know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/e/ace7328133fbaac6396a6e5fc9fa65f335320cd3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"73\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/694edce082702c815ff46702afad805ecebea666.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle CPB = 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"107\" height=\"13\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/8/3385c533d3df2fad9abfcb8afaace67fe3640b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle PBC = \\angle PCB = 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"178\" height=\"13\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> be the foot of the perpendicular from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" />. Then the area of [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />] is the same as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/6/5066be2b9379ed7ed22fbda72dd154b4e80835a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7OP$\" width=\"37\" height=\"12\" /> because base <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> has length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/820a20de2847dfdc1bc5cffc8d904933150032bd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. We can split <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> into two <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/2/1/4215ac5be49f443a5f6ba0b1e0b62d70ee0addb3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15-75-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" /> triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/a/00a3aec203d36763bff1de1788496aa77b07f34c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BOP$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/4/e84614f20f337820ee6b9dd1d2f27e74e3ca80dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$COP$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/5/8251b4d1895174deef4f32200c427530bb7aef48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BO=CO=7$\" width=\"115\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/6/6e641d320b982d3945c47c0fd2c483c61768ddb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OP=7 \\tan 15=7(2-\\sqrt{3})=14-7\\sqrt3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"314\" height=\"21\" />. Then, the area of [<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/c/fac056ce386c7154c5ed723c55b2808cc0357fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BPC$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />] is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/2/4/a248503d776780087da0662445b9e94d173bb4fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7 \\cdot OP=98-49\\sqrt{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"160\" height=\"21\" />, and so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/1/1d10b29bbeb2c303d39d9b2514e7b4f59f5e4705.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$98+49+3=\\boxed{150}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"153\" height=\"23\" />.   \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I\" title=\"2009 AIME I\">2009 AIME I</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AIME I Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2009\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b>Last Question</b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AIME_I_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2009 AIME I Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017220646\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.052 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.071 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 633/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1757/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 116/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 21089/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   12.549      1 -total\n 58.03%    7.282      1 Template:AIME_box\n 39.33%    4.936      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7998:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017220646 and revision id 289195. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}